Subject: [PATCH] Refuse unready candidate queries before global admission

Candidate commands queued behind an onboarding radio registered their global
single-flight type before they could execute. Pending commands do not start
the execution timeout, so every other agent could be rejected indefinitely.
Check both radio ownership and execution readiness under the command lock
before queuing this read-only request. Return Not_Ready without clearing the
radio owner or registering command statistics. Other command admission is
unchanged. The regression reproduces the old block for 70 ticks and exercises
occupied-ready, idle-unready and healthy-unrelated radios.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
@@ -152,6 +152,20 @@
         // if there are no candidates, complete the command
         destroy_command(pcmd);
     } else {
+        if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_unassoc_sta_query) {
+            bool ready = eligible_for_active(pcmd);
+            for (unsigned int index = 0; ready && index < queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates); ++index) {
+                auto *radio = static_cast<em_t *>(queue_peek(pcmd->m_em_candidates, index));
+                ready = radio != nullptr && is_em_ready_for_orch_exec(pcmd, radio);
+            }
+            if (!ready) {
+                while (queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates) != 0)
+                    queue_remove(pcmd->m_em_candidates, queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates) - 1);
+                pcmd->deinit();
+                delete pcmd;
+                return false;
+            }
+        }
         queue_push(m_pending, pcmd);
         push_stats(pcmd);
         unsigned int pending = queue_count(m_pending);
